course: dictionary
lesson: 5551
title: Animal words and figurative meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lemming is a small, furry rodent with a short tail. It lives in cold northern lands, such as the Arctic tundra. «Lemmings are small tundra rodents whose numbers rise and fall hugely every few years.» The clues are the words around lemmings: small, tundra and rodents.
explain: Sometimes a word is used in a picture sense, not a real one. «Like lemmings» describes people who follow each other without thinking. Ask yourself: is this about a real animal, or about how people behave?
explain: Check a story before you repeat it. «Lemmings do not jump off cliffs on purpose.» The text is correcting a myth, so the context tells you the truth. «A good scientist checks a story before repeating it.»
fact: A lemming is a small, furry, short-tailed rodent that lives in cold northern lands such as the Arctic tundra.
fact: «Like lemmings» is a figurative phrase: it means people following the crowd without thinking, even into danger.
fact: Lemming numbers rise and fall in big cycles every few years, and in crowded years they spread out.
fact: Lemmings do not jump off cliffs on purpose; a 1958 Disney film staged that scene.
fact: Arctic foxes, snowy owls and stoats all eat lemmings.
exercise: «Lemmings are small tundra rodents.» What is a lemming? | *A small, furry rodent that lives in cold northern lands | A type of fish that remembers for months | A cold, icy lake | A large bird that lives in hot deserts
exercise: Sam says, «Our class all copied the same idea, like lemmings.» What does like lemmings suggest? | People who are very small and furry | People who jump off cliffs on purpose | People who love cold weather | *People following each other without thinking
exercise: Which animal eats lemmings? | Goldfish | Bat | *Arctic fox | Ostrich
test: «Lemmings do not jump off cliffs on purpose.» What does this sentence tell you? | Cliffs are where lemmings live | *The idea that lemmings jump off cliffs is a myth | Lemmings jump off cliffs to find food | Lemmings jump off cliffs every winter
test: «In crowded years they spread out and some drown crossing rivers.» Why do lemmings spread out in crowded years? | Because they want to sing | *Because there are too many of them | Because the tundra is warm | Because they are playing a game
exam: Mia says lemmings jump off cliffs because she saw it in a film. What should she do before repeating it? | *Check it with a good source, because films can be staged | Repeat it, because films are always true | Tell everyone it is a fact | Ignore all animal stories ever
